# Kraken API configuration - SERVER SIDE ONLY
#
# `local.env` is read by the dev server (`npm run dev`) and by nothing else:
# `vite/localEnv.ts` parses it and puts its values into the server process's
# environment. `npx vercel dev` does not know this filename, and always
# simulates anyway. The values are never compiled into the browser bundle, and
# nothing in `src/` may read them.
#
# You only need this file to run LIVE trading against your own Kraken account,
# on your own machine. Without it the app runs in simulation mode, which needs
# no credentials and is safe to click through end to end.
#
# A live server signs Kraken requests for whoever can reach it, and ships no
# authentication of its own. It is therefore LOOPBACK ONLY: the dev server
# refuses to start in live mode on any bind but localhost, 127.0.0.1 or ::1, and
# the endpoints serve only a request whose peer address is loopback, whose Host
# header names one of those three, which carries this app's own header
# `X-Block-Builder-App: 1`, and which declares no other origin. Anything else is
# answered as though this deployment simulated, /api/kraken/status included, so
# a scripted caller must send the header too:
#
#     curl -s -H 'X-Block-Builder-App: 1' localhost:3002/api/kraken/status
#
# The header is not a secret and is not authentication; it is the thing a page
# on another site cannot send. Exposing a live instance beyond localhost means
# adding your own protection in front of it.
#
# The public deployment is simulation only and REFUSES to start in live mode.
# Setting these variables in a hosting dashboard does not enable live trading,
# it puts the deployment into a misconfigured state on purpose - see the
# "Trading modes" section of README.md.
#
# To generate API keys:
# 1. Log in to your Kraken account
# 2. Go to Settings > API
# 3. Create a key with the narrowest permissions you need. The authenticated
#    calls this app makes today are reads: "Query funds" covers
#    /api/kraken/balance, and "Access WebSockets API" is required for
#    /api/kraken/ws-token, because Kraken gates GetWebSocketsToken on it. Grant
#    order permissions only if you have deliberately enabled order placement.
#
# IMPORTANT: never commit your actual API keys. `local.env` is gitignored.

# Opt in to live trading. Omit this line, or set it to `simulation`, to simulate.
KRAKEN_TRADING_MODE=live

# Confirm that this process runs on your own machine. Live mode is refused
# without it, and refused anyway if the environment carries a hosting signal
# (VERCEL, AWS_LAMBDA_FUNCTION_NAME, LAMBDA_TASK_ROOT or any VERCEL_ENV).
KRAKEN_ALLOW_LOCAL_LIVE=1

KRAKEN_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
KRAKEN_API_PRIVATE_KEY=your_api_private_key_here
